    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store and compare numbers in **E.164 form**.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `normalizeTelephone` (which stripped to raw digits and required exactly 10) with `toE164`:\n- Keeps a leading `+` and country code when the input starts with `+`; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n- Strips spaces, dashes, brackets (any non-digit).\n- Requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, returning `null` (\u2192 **400 Bad Request**) when that can't be met.\n- `addOwner` now stores the returned E.164 string; `isTelephoneInUse` compares candidates against each stored number converted to E.164, so duplicate detection is on E.164 values.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 updated the Bean Validation constraint on `telephone` from `@Digits`/`@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` to `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` (and removed the now-unused `@Digits` import), so the persisted E.164 string validates instead of being rejected as not-10-digits.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` field description and example to document the E.164 normalization.\n\nVerified against the acceptance tests: `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456` (explicit country code preserved), and `12` \u2192 **400**. Full suite: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
